[[:db/cas 17592186567796 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=4x + 9 \\\\ y &=4x + 9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nThe lines corresponding to the equations {{field-1}}. Therefore, the system has {{field-2}}, meaning that it's {{field-3}}." "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=9 + 4x \\\\ y &=4x + 9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nThe lines corresponding to the equations {{field-1}}. Therefore, the system has {{field-2}}, meaning that it's {{field-3}}."] [:db/ensure 17592186567771 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186567807 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186567779 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186567796 :question/validate] {:db/id "generator-17592186198347" :question-generator/id #uuid "67f32c88-8486-5940-b96e-87ef88d4b32e" :question-generator/script "generators/da/da123f7ef3a3d73f56d896d4d39e06d5229fdcaa9ef0ad062cdd58627ff8f15b/generator.py"} [:db/cas 17592186198347 :knowledge-point/question-generator 17592186567828 "generator-17592186198347"] [:db/ensure 17592186198347 :knowledge-point/validate] [:db/cas 17592186567832 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &=-9 \\\\ -2x - 3y &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations is {{field-1}}." "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &=-9 \\\\ -4x - 6y &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system of equations is {{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186567832 :question/worked-solution "A system of equations is *consistent* if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, it is called *inconsistent*.\n\nConsistent systems, in turn, can be of the following two types:\n\n- When a system of equations has a *single* solution, it is called *consistent independent*.\n- When a system of equations has an *infinite number* of solutions, it is called *consistent dependent*.\n\nWe can summarize these definitions using the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution.\n\nFirst, we can solve the first equation for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2x &= -9 + 3y \\\\ x &= \\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation to obtain an equation that we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2\\left(\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\right) - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -9 + 3y - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -9 &= -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the system is consistent dependent." "A system of equations is *consistent* if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, it is called *inconsistent*.\n\nConsistent systems, in turn, can be of the following two types:\n\n- When a system of equations has a *single* solution, it is called *consistent independent*.\n- When a system of equations has an *infinite number* of solutions, it is called *consistent dependent*.\n\nWe can summarize these definitions using the diagram shown below.\n\n![](images/16/1692fbea298339ff839cf2f14986d51af45d1ec72b2b7d0de179336bdef40c0e.png)\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution.\n\nFirst, we can solve the first equation for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &= -9 \\\\ -2x &= -9 + 3y \\\\ x &= \\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation to obtain an equation that we can solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -4\\left(\\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}y\\right) - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -18 + 6y - 6y &= -18 \\\\ -18 &= -18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the system is consistent dependent."] [:db/ensure 17592186567839 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186567832 :question/validate] {:db/id "generator-17592186198348" :question-generator/id #uuid "3c913493-bb92-52ee-8a4c-f39ba65ce61b" :question-generator/script "generators/72/7281c419e02d8b3024558ac1486300b59c7cbd92544845b110eb82dfa2a5dc4f/generator.py"} [:db/cas 17592186198348 :knowledge-point/question-generator 17592186567854 "generator-17592186198348"] [:db/ensure 17592186198348 :knowledge-point/validate]]
